   "evidence": "The statement is `(A.submatrix (\u03c4\u2218e\u2218inr) (\u03c3\u2218e\u2218inr)).det = sign \u03c3 * sign \u03c4 * A.det * (A\u207b\u00b9.submatrix (\u03c3\u2218e\u2218inl) (\u03c4\u2218e\u2218inl)).det`. Its siblings are named `det_submatrix_comp_inr_eq_sign_mul_det_mul_det_submatrix_comp_inl` and `\u2026_of_det_eq_one`. The Mathlib convention is that a theorem name describes its conclusion.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/ComplementaryMinor.lean",
   "fix": "Name it after its conclusion, the same way as its siblings, e.g. `det_submatrix_comp_inr_eq_sign_mul_det_mul_det_submatrix_comp_inl_nonsing_inv`, or `..._det_nonsing_inv_submatrix_comp_inl`.",
   "issue": "`det_submatrix_comp_inr_nonsing_inv` suggests its conclusion is about `det (A\u207b\u00b9.submatrix (\u2026 \u2218 Sum.inr) \u2026)`. In fact the left side is a minor of `A` on `inr`, and `A\u207b\u00b9` appears only on the right, in the `inl` minor. The name leaves out the equality and the sign/det factors that its three siblings spell out.",
   "line": 173
  }
